# Everything under deploy/ is copied onto a Linux server. Checking any of it out
# with CRLF breaks it there: a shell script with CRLF fails as
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and sshd/nginx/systemd config files can pick up
# stray carriage returns that are invisible in most editors.
#
# This is not hypothetical - a stray CR in an authorized_keys line silently
# prevented key authentication during the initial bring-up of this server.
#
# Force LF regardless of the checkout platform or core.autocrlf setting.
* text eol=lf
